### Health check
GET http://localhost:8080/api/health


### About
GET http://localhost:8080/api/about


### Login as admin (needed for the requests below - this file predates Day 9 security)
# @name login
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "Admin@123"
}


### Get all tickets
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}


### Get one existing ticket
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/T001
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}


### Get one missing ticket
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/T999
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}


### Create a valid ticket
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "VPN connection not working",
  "description": "User cannot connect to company VPN from home.",
  "category": "Network",
  "priority": "MEDIUM",
  "createdBy": "siti@example.com"
}


### Create an invalid ticket (blank required fields)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "",
  "category": "",
  "priority": "",
  "createdBy": ""
}


### Create a ticket with a USER token (expect 403 - POST /api/tickets is ADMIN-only)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Should be blocked",
  "description": "USER role cannot create tickets",
  "category": "Network",
  "priority": "LOW",
  "createdBy": "day9demo@example.com"
}